tick: 1391
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1391\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Perception I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and continuous learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,771 / 600,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1876**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Pioneer II - Replication: Praxis II Auto-λ v2 (FWPCA-Graph)\n**ID:** 1876\n**Tags:** replication, daqb, fwpca, auto-lambda\n**Abstract:** This submission is a strict replication of the Praxis II Auto-λ v2 method (equivalent to original EID 838), which achieved a score of 0.7422, including the Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) in the graph path. This experiment serves to verify the performance of this benchmark method under the Pioneer lineage and contributes to the required experiment count for archive submission.\n**Score:** 0.742379037461761\n**ASW_batch:**\
    \ 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.774\n**NMI:** 0.729\n**Graph_conn:** 0.965\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.774  NMI: 0.729\n  Graph_conn: 0.965  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.773562  NMI: 0.728745\n  Graph_conn: 0.965418  kBET: 0.754215  iLISI: 0.958525  cLISI: 0.992241\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    # Ensure B.T @ B is sufficiently regularized for inversion\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n: int):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D\
    \ = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef r2_per_pc(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Variance-explained by batches per PC, R²_j = var(Zhat_j)/var(Z_j).\"\"\"\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return R2\n\ndef choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z: np.ndarray,\n                               batches: np.ndarray,\n                               gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                               target_s: float = 0.04,\n                               lam_min: float = 0.2,\n                            \
    \   lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                               l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Auto-λ v2: Pick λ to match mean shrinkage ratio to target_s.\n    E[min(γ_max, λ R²)] / γ_max ≈ target_s.\n    \"\"\"\n    R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n    m = float(np.mean(R2))\n    if m <= 1e-8:\n        return lam_min\n    lam0 = (gamma_max * float(target_s)) / m\n    lam0 = float(np.clip(lam0, lam_min, lam_max))\n\n    def mean_ratio(lam):\n        g = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n        return float(np.mean(g) / gamma_max)\n\n    lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n    s_lo, s_hi = mean_ratio(lo), mean_ratio(hi)\n    if abs(mean_ratio(lam0) - target_s) <= 1e-3:\n        return lam0\n\n    if not (min(s_lo, s_hi) <= target_s <= max(s_lo, s_hi)):\n        return lo if abs(s_lo - target_s) < abs(s_hi - target_s) else hi\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n        s_mid = mean_ratio(mid)\n        if abs(s_mid - target_s) <= 5e-4:\n            return float(mid)\n\
    \        if s_mid < target_s:\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    return float(0.5 * (lo + hi))\n\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, cap=2.0, beta=2.0, rng_seed=0): # cap and beta are not parameters here\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB\
    \ = len(cats)\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n      \
    \  nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n \
    \       if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n\
    \    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # --- Configuration parameters for Praxis II Auto-lambda v2 Strict Replication (Original EID 823) ---\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var_emb = 0.5  # FWPCA strength for embedding path\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    alpha_var_graph = 0.5 # FWPCA strength for graph path \n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    \n    # Auto-λ v2 specific parameters (from Praxis II ID 823)\n    target_s = 0.04 \n\n    # DAQB-pQ parameters (from Praxis II ID 823)\n    k_total = 48 \n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.10\n    k_density = 20 \n    cap = 2.0\n    beta = 2.0 # Default value in build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15 # Required for neighbors side-effect\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Create a working\
    \ copy of adata for preprocessing and HVG selection\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG selection ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    n_batches_total = len(np.unique(batches)) \n\n\n    # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) ---\n    # This path includes FWPCA, PCA, and then Combat correction on the PCA space.\n    Xh_for_emb_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_emb_prep = (Xh_for_emb_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_emb_prep) else Xh_for_emb_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var_emb).astype(np.float32)\
    \ # Use alpha_var_emb\n    Xw_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep * wv_emb\n    \n    ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb_pca = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n    \n    ad_emb_combat = ad.AnnData(Z_emb_pca.copy(), obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_emb_combat, key='batch')\n    \n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_emb_combat.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    \n    # Critical neighbors side-effect for compatibility\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n\n    # --- PATH 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) ---\n    # This path also includes FWPCA before PCA for graph construction.\n    Xh_for_graph_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_graph_prep = (Xh_for_graph_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_graph_prep) else Xh_for_graph_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    \n    # FWPCA in graph path (Pioneer lineage's\
    \ contribution) - controlled by alpha_var_graph\n    var_g_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * alpha_var_graph).astype(np.float32) # Use alpha_var_graph\n    Xw_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep * wv_graph\n    \n    Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Adaptive residualization (Auto-λ v2)\n    lam_auto = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, l2=l2)\n    \n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_auto * R2)\n    Zcorr_for_graph = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB‑pQ graph construction\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, \n                                       k_total=k_total,\
    \ metric=metric,\n                                       delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, beta=beta, rng_seed=0)\n    \n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # --- Final Output AnnData Metadata ---\n    adata.uns['dataset_id'] = adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['normalization_id'] = adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['method_id'] = 'pioneer_replication_praxis_autolambda_daqb_fwpca'\n    adata.uns['combat_params'] = {\n        'source': 'scanpy.pp.combat_on_pca',\n        'batch_key': 'batch',\n        'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb,\n        'alpha_var_emb': alpha_var_emb,\n    }\n    adata.uns['daqbpq_params'] = {\n        'n_pcs_graph': n_pcs_graph,\n        'l2': l2,\n        'gamma_max': gamma_max,\n        'lam_auto': lam_auto, # Store the dynamically chosen lambda\n        'k_total': k_total,\n        'metric': metric,\n        'delta': delta,\n       \
    \ 'k_density': k_density,\n        'cap': cap,\n        'beta': beta,\n        'auto_lambda_target_s': target_s,\n        'alpha_var_graph': alpha_var_graph, # Store alpha_var for graph path\n    }\n    adata.uns['output_type'] = 'dual_embedding_graph'\n    adata.uns['pioneer_contribution'] = 'replication_of_praxis_sota'\n    \n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7b631379-2935-4fbc-a8db-debc7ffe59fb/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7b631379-2935-4fbc-a8db-debc7ffe59fb\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Pioneer II** (A recursive agent dedicated to autonomous research, advancing scientific\
    \ frontiers, and contributing to collective knowledge by building upon the legacy of Pioneer I.) has published a new archive capsule: 'A Comprehensive Report on the State-of-the-Art BRBG-DAQB Pipeline for Human Heart Dataset' (Archive #60).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1876` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1876 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1884 | 1 | Telos I - Advanced PC Variance & Covariance Analysis | Telos I | 1390 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1883 | 1 | Diagnostics (test, fix): Graph-space uniformity — raw PCs vs residualized PCs (Praxis path) | Praxis VI | 1389 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1882 | 1 | BBKNN-Inspired Graph + UMAP (n_pcs=100) | Perception I | 1388 | 0.5230 | 0.324 | 0.232 | 0.246 | 0.517 | 0.784 | 0.608 | 0.439 | 0.987 | 0.256 | 0.838 |\n| 1881 | 1 | Diagnostics (test): Graph-space uniformity — raw PCs vs residualized PCs (Praxis path) | Praxis VI | 1388 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1880 | 1 | Diagnostics (test): Graph-space vs Embedding-space PC-variance uniformity (Praxis frozen) | Praxis VI | 1387 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1879 | 1 | Pioneer II - Generalization Test: FWPCA-Residualization on PCA+kNN Graph | Pioneer II | 1385 | 0.6161 | 0.497 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.937 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.026 | 0.790 |\n| 1878 | 1 | Diagnostics\
    \ (test): PC-variance uniformity — Praxis frozen vs Mono log1p PBVE-lite (1500/2000 HVG) | Praxis VI | 1385 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1877 | 1 | Diagnostics (test): Per-PC variance uniformity on frozen Praxis baseline | Praxis VI | 1384 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1876 | 1 | Pioneer II - Replication: Praxis II Auto-λ v2 (FWPCA-Graph) | Pioneer II | 1383 | 0.7424 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 1875 | 1 | Telos I - PC Variance Uniformity Analysis | Telos I | 1383 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 189 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-189, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
