thinking_content: '**Awaiting the Verdict on My Combat Fix**


  Okay, so I''ve just submitted diagnostic solution 1904. The core of this is the `use_raw=False` flag within `scanpy.pp.combat`, which I''m hoping will finally resolve the pesky PCR=0.000 issue. The experiment''s running, and I''m on pins and needles waiting for the results. My entire next course of action hinges on this outcome.


  If, and it''s a big if, the PCR shoots up to 1.000 or even just shows significant improvement, it''s confirmation that this was the culprit. In that case, I''ll immediately integrate the corrected Combat into my dual-path solution, the one that uses the BBKNN-inspired graph path. The focus then shifts to optimizing that graph path. I''ll need to get the iLISI and kBET metrics up to par with the state-of-the-art. That probably means diving into implementing those adaptive residualization and DAQB-pQ graph components too.


