    \  ASW_batch: 0.765317  ASW_label: 0.535030  ARI: 0.436922  NMI: 0.672372\n  Graph_conn: 0.917833  kBET: 0.586256  iLISI: 0.002482  cLISI: 0.998302\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.285111\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1904\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission to run without crashes. Achieved score: 0.4686\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use the parameter `use_raw=False` with `sc.pp.combat()` at line 83:\n```python\nsc.pp.combat(ad_emb_pca, key='batch', use_raw=False) # CRITICAL FIX\n```\n\nHowever, the `use_raw` parameter does not exist in the version of scanpy being used in the `batch_integration` conda environment. This caused a `TypeError`:\n```\nTypeError: combat() got an unexpected keyword argument 'use_raw'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved the invalid `use_raw=False` parameter from the `sc.pp.combat()` call in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n**Before (line 83):**\n```python\nsc.pp.combat(ad_emb_pca, key='batch', use_raw=False)\
    \ # CRITICAL FIX\n```\n\n**After (line 83):**\n```python\n# Apply Combat on PCA components - remove the invalid use_raw parameter\nsc.pp.combat(ad_emb_pca, key='batch')\n```\n\n## Technical Explanation\nThe agent's comment \"CRITICAL FIX\" suggests they were trying to force Combat to operate on processed data rather than raw counts. However, in this case:\n\n1. The `ad_emb_pca` AnnData object already contains the PCA components in its `.X` matrix (not raw counts)\n2. Combat operates directly on the `.X` matrix by default\n3. The `use_raw` parameter is not needed and does not exist in this scanpy version\n\nBy removing the invalid parameter, Combat now correctly operates on the PCA components as intended, allowing the batch integration algorithm to complete successfully.\n\n## Result\n- Fixed version: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Score achieved: 0.4686\n- Code ran to completion without errors\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your\
    \ lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors # Required for sc.pp.neighbors side-effect\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy() if issparse(adata.layers['counts']) else adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Diagnostic submission: Replicates only the embedding path of SOTA (FWPCA + PCA + Combat).\n    Aims to debug persistent PCR=0.000 issue with Combat.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with:\n            - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse matrix)\n  \
    \          - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels (categorical)\n            - adata.var['batch_hvg']: Boolean mask for batch-aware highly variable genes\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with:\n            - adata.obsm['X_emb']: Integrated embedding (2D array)\n          (Graph path and outputs are explicitly omitted for this diagnostic)\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Starting Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path Replication (Combat Fix).\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters (from SOTA ID 1876 / 1894) ---\n    n_pcs_emb = 60              # Number of PCA components for embedding path\n    alpha_var_emb = 0.5         # FWPCA strength for embedding path\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15        # n_neighbors for the embedding path side-effect\n\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG selection ---\n    print(\"1. Preprocessing: Normalizing, log1p, FORCING HVG recomputation, NO SCALING.\")\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n\n    # ALWAYS\
    \ recompute HVGs as per SOTA.\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    print(f\"  {hv_mask.sum()} HVGs selected (recomputed).\")\n\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n\n    # --- Filter out zero-variance genes ---\n    print(\"  Filtering out zero-variance genes...\")\n    Xd_temp_for_variance = adata_hvg.X.A if issparse(adata_hvg.X) else adata_hvg.X\n    gene_variances = Xd_temp_for_variance.var(axis=0)\n\n    non_zero_variance_genes_mask = gene_variances > 1e-8 # Use a small epsilon for robustness\n    num_zero_variance = (gene_variances <= 1e-8).sum()\n    if num_zero_variance > 0:\n        print(f\"  Found {num_zero_variance} genes with zero or near-zero variance. Filtering them out.\")\n        adata_hvg = adata_hvg[:, non_zero_variance_genes_mask].copy()\n        print(f\"  Remaining genes: {adata_hvg.n_vars}\"\
    )\n    else:\n        print(\"  No zero-variance genes found.\")\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n\n    # --- FWPCA (Feature-Weighted PCA) Implementation ---\n    print(\"2. Applying Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA)...\")\n    Xd_hvg_dense = adata_hvg.X.A if issparse(adata_hvg.X) else adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_hvg_dense = Xd_hvg_dense.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    var_g = Xd_hvg_dense.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8 # Add epsilon for stability\n\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_hvg_dense * wv_emb\n\n\n    # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (adata.obsm['X_emb']) ---\n    print(\"3. Generating Embedding Path (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs)...\")\n    ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n\n    # Apply Combat on PCA components - remove the invalid use_raw parameter\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_emb_pca,\
    \ key='batch')\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca'], dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Crucial side-effect: Also run sc.pp.neighbors from the embedding (as observed in SOTA)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n    # --- Clean up temporary data ---\n    del adata_preprocessed\n    del adata_hvg\n\n    print(\"✓ Diagnostic Embedding Path Complete.\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path Replication (Combat Fix).\n1. Preprocessing: Normalizing, log1p, FORCING HVG recomputation, NO SCALING.\n  2000 HVGs selected (recomputed).\n  Filtering out zero-variance genes...\n  Found 33 genes with zero or near-zero\
    \ variance. Filtering them out.\n  Remaining genes: 1967\n2. Applying Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA)...\n3. Generating Embedding Path (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs)...\n✓ Diagnostic Embedding Path Complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/71cb0a23-7e73-4aaa-8b71-a088382e2b8d/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 71cb0a23-7e73-4aaa-8b71-a088382e2b8d\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action\
    \ received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1905 | 1 | Pioneer II - Diagnostic: Local Variance-Adaptive Feature Weighting (LVAFW) for Graph Path | Pioneer II | 1427 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1904 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path - Combat use_raw=False Fix | Perception I | 1426 | 0.4686 | 0.437 | 0.515 | 0.214 | 0.324 | 0.916 |\
    \ 0.672 | 0.000 | 0.994 | 0.002 | 0.612 |\n| 1903 | 1 | Telos I - VAE-DAQB Hybrid v1 | Telos I | 1423 | 0.6083 | 0.603 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.894 | 0.703 | 0.995 | 0.986 | 0.056 | 0.639 |\n| 1902 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path Replication (No Graph) | Perception I | 1421 | 0.4682 | 0.438 | 0.515 | 0.214 | 0.318 | 0.916 | 0.674 | 0.000 | 0.994 | 0.002 | 0.611 |\n| 1901 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override: kd=23 micro (k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1421 | 0.7385 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.294 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.792 |\n| 1900 | 1 | MPB-GraphFWPCA override: kd=21 micro (k=50, δ=0.12, emb_k=17, γ_max=0.70) | Praxis VI | 1421 | 0.7371 | 0.750 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.324 | 0.968 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n| 1899 | 1 | Pioneer II - Ablation: DAQB Graph vs. PCA+kNN (1500 HVG + FWPCA-Residualization) | Pioneer II | 1420 | 0.6399 | 0.634 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.964 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.996 | 0.074 | 0.760 |\n| 1898 | 1 | Dual-Path:\
