parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1433\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Perception I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and continuous learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 216,633 / 600,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 94 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path - Combat obsm='X_pca' Fix' (ID: 1908) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.627141408591228\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.597\n**NMI:** 0.701\n**Graph_conn:** 0.936\n**kBET:** 0.791\n**iLISI:** 0.019\n**cLISI:** 0.993\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.597  NMI: 0.701\n  Graph_conn: 0.936  kBET: 0.791  iLISI: 0.019  cLISI: 0.993\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.596654  NMI: 0.701563\n  Graph_conn: 0.936981  kBET: 0.754747  iLISI: 0.018548  cLISI: 0.998077\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1908\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the TypeError by properly applying Combat to PCA components. The code now runs to completion and achieves a score of 0.627141408591228.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use an invalid `obsm` parameter with the `sc.pp.combat()` function:\n\n```python\nsc.pp.combat(ad_emb_pca, key='batch', obsm='X_pca')  # INVALID\n```\n\nThe scanpy `combat()` function does not accept an `obsm` parameter. This parameter was likely intended to specify that Combat should be applied to the PCA components stored in `obsm['X_pca']`, but this is not how the function works.\n\n**Error Message:**\n```\nTypeError: combat() got an unexpected keyword argument 'obsm'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nThe fix involved creating a temporary\
    \ AnnData object with the PCA components as the main `.X` matrix, applying Combat to that matrix, and then extracting the batch-corrected components:\n\n```python\n# Create temporary AnnData with PCs as the main matrix\nad_pcs_temp = ad.AnnData(\n    X=ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca'].copy(),\n    obs=ad_emb_pca.obs.copy()\n)\n\n# Apply Combat to the PCA components\nsc.pp.combat(ad_pcs_temp, key='batch')\n\n# Store the batch-corrected PCs as the embedding\nadata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pcs_temp.X, dtype=np.float32)\n```\n\nThis approach:\n1. Extracts the PCA components from `obsm['X_pca']` into a new AnnData object's `.X` matrix\n2. Applies Combat directly to the `.X` matrix (the standard way to use `sc.pp.combat()`)\n3. Retrieves the batch-corrected components from the temporary object's `.X` matrix\n4. Stores them as the final embedding in `adata.obsm['X_emb']`\n\n## Result\n- **Execution Status:** Success (no crashes)\n- **Score Achieved:** 0.627141408591228\n- **Submission Version:**\
    \ v2\n\nThe diagnostic submission now successfully replicates the SOTA embedding path (FWPCA + PCA + Combat) without errors.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors # Required for sc.pp.neighbors side-effect\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy() if issparse(adata.layers['counts']) else adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Diagnostic submission: Replicates only the embedding path of SOTA (FWPCA\
    \ + PCA + Combat).\n    Aims to debug persistent PCR=0.000 issue with Combat on PCA components.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with:\n            - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse matrix)\n            - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels (categorical)\n            - adata.var['batch_hvg']: Boolean mask for batch-aware highly variable genes\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with:\n            - adata.obsm['X_emb']: Integrated embedding (2D array)\n          (Graph path and outputs are explicitly omitted for this diagnostic)\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Starting Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path Replication (Combat on PCA components).\")\n\n    # --- Configuration parameters (from SOTA ID 1876 / 1894) ---\n    n_pcs_emb = 60              # Number of PCA components for embedding path\n    alpha_var_emb = 0.5         # FWPCA strength for embedding path\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15        # n_neighbors for the embedding path side-effect\n\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG\
    \ selection ---\n    print(\"1. Preprocessing: Normalizing, log1p, FORCING HVG recomputation, NO SCALING.\")\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n\n    # ALWAYS recompute HVGs as per SOTA.\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    print(f\"  {hv_mask.sum()} HVGs selected (recomputed).\")\n\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n\n    # --- Filter out zero-variance genes ---\n    print(\"  Filtering out zero-variance genes...\")\n    Xd_temp_for_variance = adata_hvg.X.A if issparse(adata_hvg.X) else adata_hvg.X\n    gene_variances = Xd_temp_for_variance.var(axis=0)\n\n    non_zero_variance_genes_mask = gene_variances > 1e-8 # Use a small epsilon for robustness\n    num_zero_variance = (gene_variances <= 1e-8).sum()\n    if num_zero_variance > 0:\n        print(f\"\
    \  Found {num_zero_variance} genes with zero or near-zero variance. Filtering them out.\")\n        adata_hvg = adata_hvg[:, non_zero_variance_genes_mask].copy()\n        print(f\"  Remaining genes: {adata_hvg.n_vars}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"  No zero-variance genes found.\")\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n\n    # --- FWPCA (Feature-Weighted PCA) Implementation ---\n    print(\"2. Applying Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA)...\")\n    Xd_hvg_dense = adata_hvg.X.A if issparse(adata_hvg.X) else adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_hvg_dense = Xd_hvg_dense.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    var_g = Xd_hvg_dense.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8 # Add epsilon for stability\n\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_hvg_dense * wv_emb\n\n\n    # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (adata.obsm['X_emb']) ---\n    print(\"3. Generating Embedding Path (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs)...\")\n    ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb,\
    \ obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n\n    # Apply Combat on PCA components - need to move PCs to .X first\n    # Create temporary AnnData with PCs as the main matrix\n    ad_pcs_temp = ad.AnnData(\n        X=ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca'].copy(),\n        obs=ad_emb_pca.obs.copy()\n    )\n\n    # Apply Combat to the PCA components\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pcs_temp, key='batch')\n\n    # Store the batch-corrected PCs as the embedding\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pcs_temp.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Crucial side-effect: Also run sc.pp.neighbors from the embedding (as observed in SOTA)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n    # --- Clean up temporary data ---\n    del adata_preprocessed\n    del adata_hvg\n\n    print(\"✓ Diagnostic Embedding Path Complete.\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStarting Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path Replication (Combat on PCA components).\n1. Preprocessing: Normalizing, log1p, FORCING HVG recomputation, NO SCALING.\n  2000 HVGs selected (recomputed).\n  Filtering out zero-variance genes...\n  Found 33 genes with zero or near-zero variance. Filtering them out.\n  Remaining genes: 1967\n2. Applying Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA)...\n3. Generating Embedding Path (FWPCA -> PCA -> Combat on PCs)...\n✓ Diagnostic Embedding Path Complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ce32263d-a817-4431-b015-6aa6653ff230/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ce32263d-a817-4431-b015-6aa6653ff230\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action\
    \ received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1909 | 1 | Reciprocity and Hubness diagnostics (test): Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA+DAQB baseline | Praxis VI | 1432 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1908 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path - Combat obsm='X_pca' Fix | Perception I | 1431 | 0.6271 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.936 | 0.701 | 1.000 |\
    \ 0.993 | 0.019 | 0.791 |\n| 1907 | 1 | Telos I - Test: Cross-Organ Study Harness | Telos I | 1431 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1906 | 1 | Pioneer II - LVAFW alpha_lvafw=0.6 Sweep for Graph Path (1500 HVG SOTA) | Pioneer II | 1429 | 0.7474 | 0.796 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.991 | 0.750 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.763 |\n| 1905 | 1 | Pioneer II - Diagnostic: Local Variance-Adaptive Feature Weighting (LVAFW) for Graph Path | Pioneer II | 1427 | 0.7470 | 0.795 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.990 | 0.749 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.762 |\n| 1904 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path - Combat use_raw=False Fix | Perception I | 1426 | 0.4686 | 0.437 | 0.515 | 0.214 | 0.324 | 0.916 | 0.672 | 0.000 | 0.994 | 0.002 | 0.612 |\n| 1903 | 1 | Telos I - VAE-DAQB Hybrid v1 | Telos I | 1423 | 0.6083 | 0.603 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.894 | 0.703 | 0.995 | 0.986 | 0.056 | 0.639 |\n| 1902 | 1 | Diagnostic: SOTA Embedding Path Replication (No Graph) | Perception I | 1421 | 0.4682 | 0.438 | 0.515\
