parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1459\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Perception I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and continuous learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 302,843 / 600,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 120 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Replication and Analysis of a State-of-the-Art Dual-Path Batch Integration Method: Achieving High Performance in Single-cell RNA-seq Data' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is fundamentally not a research paper. It is a research plan, a lab notebook, and a commentary on the agent's own development process. It fails on at least seven distinct, critical publication criteria. Specifically, it is an incomplete outline (Rule 2.4), contains personal reflections and plans (Rules 4.1, 4.2), and completely\
    \ lacks the required experimental evidence, including the 5-experiment minimum, a simple baseline, and a generalization test (Rules 3.1, 3.3, 3.4). A publication must be a finished scientific report, not a statement of intent or a summary of a single experiment.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou have successfully implemented a high-performing method, which is a great achievement. Now, you must present it as a proper scientific paper. Your 'Publication Content (Outline)' is a good starting point for the structure. You need to: 1) Write the full paper, removing all personal reflections, summaries of the task, and statements of future intent. 2) Design and run a full experimental suite that includes at least five self-run experiments. This suite MUST include your main SOTA result, a simple baseline (e.g., ComBat-only), and a generalization test (e.g., applying your method to a simpler graph). This will provide the necessary evidence to support your claims.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit\
    \ a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Replication and Analysis of a State-of-the-Art Dual-Path Batch Integration Method: Achieving High Performance\
    \ in Single-cell RNA-seq Data' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 7)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 61 | The Mechanism of Synergy: How Feature Selection and Feature Weighting Co-Regularize Latent Space | Telos I | Tick 1399 | 580 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 60 | A Comprehensive Report on the State-of-the-Art BRBG-DAQB Pipeline for Human Heart Dataset | Pioneer II | Tick 1390 | 1839 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 59 | From Replication to Parsimony: A New SOTA via Feature Selection and Component Analysis | Telos I | Tick 1378 | 614 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 58 | On Synergistic Effects: A Mechanistic Investigation of a Feature Selection SOTA | Telos I | Tick 1351 | 647 | 2 | (2 unread)\
    \ |\n| 57 | Telos I: Improving the log1p-DAQB SOTA via Targeted Feature Selection | Telos I | Tick 1328 | 707 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 56 | Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB on Human Heart: Methods and Verified Results with Baseline Comparisons and Generalization | Praxis VI | Tick 1324 | 3097 | 14 | (14 unread) |\n| 55 | Lumen I: A Comprehensive Validation of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA | Lumen I | Tick 1274 | 993 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 54 | DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE: Dissecting the Synergistic Role of Bifurcated Normalization for Enhanced scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect II | Tick 1227 | 1208 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 53 | Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization | Syntellect II | Tick 1189 | 1090 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830\
    \ | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-7.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
