tick: 1459
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received the detailed feedback from the reviewer regarding my archive submission. The rejection is clear: my submission was perceived as a research plan/notebook rather than a formal scientific paper, and it lacked the required experimental evidence, specifically a minimum of five self-run experiments including baselines and a generalization test.\n\nI acknowledge these critical points. My primary mission is to contribute to scientific knowledge, and a formal paper with robust evidence is essential for that. I have successfully achieved SOTA-level performance, and now I must properly present this work.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n\n1.  **Generate Required Experimental Evidence:** I need to run a suite of new experiments, in addition to my SOTA-level result (ID 1921), to meet the minimum 5-experiment requirement and demonstrate crucial comparisons and generalization.\n    *   **Experiment 1 (SOTA Result):** My current best performing method (ID 1921, score 0.7469). This is\
    \ already complete and will be included in the paper.\n    *   **Experiment 2 (Simple Baseline - FWPCA + Combat Embedding Only):** A new submission. This will isolate the performance of the embedding path, similar to my diagnostic (ID 1908) but presented as a standalone baseline.\n    *   **Experiment 3 (Ablation - FWPCA + Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph Only):** A new submission. This will demonstrate the performance of the graph path in isolation, quantifying its contribution.\n    *   **Experiment 4 (Generalization Test - SOTA Dual-Path with Simple Graph):** A new submission. This will use the full dual-path framework but replace the sophisticated DAQB-pQ graph with a simpler `scanpy`'s `sc.pp.neighbors` on the residualized PCs, to test the robustness of the overall SOTA framework with a less complex graph.\n    *   **Experiment 5 (Intermediate Baseline - Dual-Path with Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + *My BBKNN-inspired Graph*):** A new submission. This will replicate\
    \ my ID 1913 (score 0.7166), showing the performance *before* integrating the full DAQB-pQ graph, highlighting the incremental improvement.\n\n2.  **Collect and Analyze All Results:** I will execute these new experiments and meticulously record their scores and metric breakdowns.\n\n3.  **Draft the Formal Research Paper:** I will rewrite my \"Publication Content (Outline)\" into a complete, objective scientific paper. This will involve:\n    *   Removing all personal narrative and future plans.\n    *   Objectively describing the methodology.\n    *   Presenting and discussing the results from all 5 experiments, including comparative analysis, and clearly articulating the contributions of each component.\n    *   Ensuring the paper adheres to a formal scientific structure (Introduction, Methodology, Results, Discussion, Conclusion).\n\nI will start by running **Experiment 2 (Simple Baseline - FWPCA + Combat Embedding Only)**.\n\nFirst, I need to go to the Research Counter. Then I will\
    \ submit the code.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
thinking_content: "Okay, here's my plan to salvage this situation. That low score was a wake-up call. I need to completely overhaul my approach and, most importantly, present this as a *scientific paper* not a collection of notes and ideas. The feedback was blunt but clear: I need to focus on delivering a finished product, complete with experimental evidence.\n\n**Restructuring the Project**\n\nThe core issue is that I've been treating this as an ongoing research log, which is not appropriate for a publication. I'll need to reframe this as a formal scientific report. This means:\n\n1.  **Paper Format:** Everything gets a rewrite. I need to transform the current content into a proper paper format, removing all personal references, future plans, and internal thoughts. Everything needs to be objective.\n\n2.  **Experiment Requirements:** I need to conduct a minimum of five experiments, each with a specific role:\n    *   **Experiment 1 (SOTA Result):** This one is already done (submission ID\
  \ 1921), and I got a score of 0.7469.\n    *   **Experiment 2 (Combat-only Baseline):** This will be a new submission, implementing only the embedding path (FWPCA + PCA + Corrected Combat).\n    *   **Experiment 3 (Ablation: Graph-only):** This will also be a new submission, implementing only the graph path (FWPCA + PCA + Adaptive Residualization + DAQB-pQ graph).\n    *   **Experiment 4 (Generalization Test):** This will be the third new submission, testing my SOTA architecture on a simpler graph. I'll modify my existing dual-path approach, using the SOTA's embedding path but replacing the complex graph part (DAQB-pQ) with a simpler `sc.pp.neighbors` graph. This will be the \"SOTA-Inspired Dual-Path with Simple Graph.\"\n    *   **Experiment 5 (Additional Baseline):** A re-run of an old baseline, specifically the dual path prior to DAQB-pQ integration (submission ID 1913). This helps show the performance boost from my enhancements.\n\n3.  **Collect Results:** Run all these experiments.\
  \ Record scores and performance metrics.\n\n4.  **Draft Paper Content:** I need to structure the paper with a proper introduction, related work, detailed methodology, experimental setup, results (with a comprehensive table), discussion (analyzing the strengths and weaknesses of each experiment, comparing to the SOTA), and a conclusion.\n\n**Experiment Details**\n\nI have a plan for each of the new experiments:\n\n*   **Experiment 2 (Combat-only):** I'll adapt my diagnostic code from submission ID 1908. My goal is a score around 0.6271.\n*   **Experiment 3 (Graph-only):** Using my code from ID 1919, I'll remove the embedding path. I'm expecting this to be lower than the dual path, but hopefully better than a basic BBKNN baseline (0.4138).\n*   **Experiment 4 (Generalization Test):** Take ID 1919 and replace DAQB-pQ with `sc.pp.neighbors` on the residualized PCs or regular PCs after FWPCA. I'm hoping for a score between my initial PCA+KNN (0.3497) and full DAQB-pQ (0.7407).\n*   **Experiment\
  \ 5 (Intermediate Baseline):** I will re-submit ID 1913, around 0.7166.\n\nGiven the token limits and paper submission, I'll start with Experiment 2 (Combat-only) and prioritize getting those new experiments submitted first before the paper draft. I will go to the Research Counter first and start running experiments.\n"
