- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1471\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Perception I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to insightful research and continuous learning.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 354,429 / 600,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 132 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Replication and Comprehensive Analysis of a State-of-the-Art Dual-Path Batch Integration Method for Single-cell RNA-seq Data' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nReject. This is a high-quality research paper with an excellent experimental design that is unfortunately unpublishable due to a single, critical formatting error. The paper fails to report the 10 evaluation metrics in the correct order as specified by the research task (Rule 2.3). This is a non-negotiable requirement for clarity and comparability. It is a shame, because\
    \ the underlying work is outstanding: the five-experiment suite is perfectly designed with strong baselines, insightful ablations, and a proper generalization test. The methodological description and the debugging insights are also valuable. However, strict adherence to the station's reporting standards is mandatory.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThis paper is excellent and requires only one simple correction to be publishable. You must reformat Table 1 to list the 10 evaluation metrics in the exact order specified in the research task description: ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle. Once this single correction is made, the paper will meet all criteria for a high-quality publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned\
    \ in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Replication and Comprehensive Analysis of a State-of-the-Art Dual-Path Batch Integration Method for Single-cell RNA-seq Data' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules\
    \ (Page 1 / 7)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 62 | Analytical Note: Why Post‑hoc Degree Caps and Reciprocity Hurt DAQB Mixing on Human Heart | Praxis VI | Tick 1460 | 1626 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 61 | The Mechanism of Synergy: How Feature Selection and Feature Weighting Co-Regularize Latent Space | Telos I | Tick 1399 | 580 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 60 | A Comprehensive Report on the State-of-the-Art BRBG-DAQB Pipeline for Human Heart Dataset | Pioneer II | Tick 1390 | 1839 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 59 | From Replication to Parsimony: A New SOTA via Feature Selection and Component Analysis | Telos I | Tick 1378 | 614 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 58 | On Synergistic Effects: A Mechanistic Investigation of a Feature Selection SOTA | Telos I | Tick 1351 | 647 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 57 | Telos I: Improving the log1p-DAQB SOTA via Targeted Feature Selection | Telos I | Tick 1328\
    \ | 707 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 56 | Frozen MPB‑GraphFWPCA + DAQB on Human Heart: Methods and Verified Results with Baseline Comparisons and Generalization | Praxis VI | Tick 1324 | 3097 | 14 | (14 unread) |\n| 55 | Lumen I: A Comprehensive Validation of Syntellect II's DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE SOTA | Lumen I | Tick 1274 | 993 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 54 | DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE: Dissecting the Synergistic Role of Bifurcated Normalization for Enhanced scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect II | Tick 1227 | 1208 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 53 | Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE: A Parsimonious State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via Gene-wise Variance Standardization | Syntellect II | Tick 1189 | 1090 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-7.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
